---
/**
 * HiloTricolor (design-system.md §7.12, item 12; design/ds/canvas/Elementos.dc.html
 * block "HILOTRICOLOR"): a 3px line in three equal solid thirds — yellow /
 * blue / red, the only place in the whole UI where the Venezuelan tricolor
 * appears in full (design-system.md §3.3, "tricolor solo en HiloTricolor...
 * nunca como fondo, botón o acento de UI"). Detail of `Pie` (SM-028) or of a
 * future edition badge, never a generic section divider.
 *
 * The three colors are fixed and carry no props (backlog SM-024, "sin props
 * de color"; PLAN.md §5, "el tricolor es fijo"): the `.hilo-tricolor` class
 * in theme.css supplies the 3px height and the hard-stopped gradient that
 * renders as three solid blocks. `ancho` (PLAN.md §5) is the only prop, for
 * a narrower badge use case; it is applied as an inline style because
 * Tailwind's `w-*` utilities need a literal class string at build time and
 * cannot take an arbitrary value from a runtime prop.
 *
 * Purely decorative — it carries no information of its own — so it is
 * `aria-hidden`.
 *
 * `entrada` turns on the left-to-right `clip-path` sweep of design-system.md
 * §11.4 by emitting `data-entrada="hilo"`, whose keyframes and two mandatory
 * guards live in theme.css. It is a prop, not a default, because §11.4 scopes
 * the sweep to the `Pie` — "Solo en el `Pie` (una vez por página)" — while a
 * future edition badge uses the same component and must stay static. `Pie.astro`
 * is the only caller that passes it. Sweeping with `clip-path` (never
 * `transform`) is §11.6's rule 3, and the line is fully painted from the first
 * frame on a browser without scroll-driven animations or under reduced motion,
 * since nothing here starts clipped outside that block.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN: §11.4 marks this sweep as "sujeto a prueba en dispositivo: si se
 * lee como barra de carga, queda estático". That test is Ruben's, on a real
 * phone; if it reads as a progress bar, the fix is dropping `entrada` from the
 * single `<HiloTricolor>` in `Pie.astro` — no CSS change needed.
 *
 * No position classes are accepted here (diseno-web-indice.md, decision 13):
 * a caller that needs to place this within a layout wraps it instead.
 */
interface Props {
  /** CSS width value. Defaults to 100%, the `Pie` use case. */
  ancho?: string;
  /** Turns on the `clip-path` sweep of design-system.md §11.4 (`data-entrada="hilo"`). Only the `Pie`'s single instance passes it. Defaults to `false`. */
  entrada?: boolean;
}

const { ancho = '100%', entrada = false } = Astro.props;
---

<div
  class="hilo-tricolor"
  aria-hidden="true"
  data-entrada={entrada ? 'hilo' : undefined}
  style={`width: ${ancho};`}
>
</div>
